WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.436
- Welcome back, everybody.
(audience cheers)

00:00:01.436 --> 00:00:03.597
We've got Arnold Schwarzenegger here

00:00:03.597 --> 00:00:06.690
and Paul Shaffer along
with our band, y'all.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.370
Our next guests live on one

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:10.440
of the most famous streets in the world,

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.500
where children grow smarter,
stronger, and kinder.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.040
You can join them for season
54 of "Sesame Street."

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.470
It premiers November 9th on Max.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:22.967
Everybody please say hello
to Elmo and Oscar the Grouch!

00:00:22.967 --> 00:00:23.800
(audience cheers)

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.327
(upbeat rock music)

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:28.160
- Hi everybody!
- Hey,

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.224
knock it off with all
the cheering will ya?

00:00:31.224 --> 00:00:33.934
Don't you know a Grouch is in the house?

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:35.299
- What's up, Arnold,
(audience cheers)

00:00:35.299 --> 00:00:37.164
have you ever met anyone
on "Sesame Street"?

00:00:37.164 --> 00:00:38.760
Have you ever met anybody?

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.630
- Well, they're good
looking characters, amazing.

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:42.060
(audience laughs)

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.710
- [Elmo] You too, Mr. Schwarzenegger.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.090
- So Elmo, I heard

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:47.010
that you have a question
for Arnold, right?

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:47.952
- Yes, Elmo does.

00:00:47.952 --> 00:00:49.523
Elmo wanted to know that,

00:00:49.523 --> 00:00:53.280
how can Elmo be strong
and healthy just like you?

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.113
- Cabbage.

00:00:54.113 --> 00:00:55.270
- Well, I mean. (laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:56.103
- [Elmo] Okay.

00:00:56.103 --> 00:00:57.458
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:57.458 --> 00:01:01.080
- Very good, but the
most important thing is,

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.100
did you eat well?

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:02.933
- Okay.

00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:06.030
- A lot of vegetables, a lot of fruits?

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:07.680
And did you exercise every day?

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:08.513
- Oh, yes, okay.

00:01:08.513 --> 00:01:10.486
- And you developed the discipline, okay?

00:01:10.486 --> 00:01:11.684
(audience laughs)

00:01:11.684 --> 00:01:14.133
- (puffs) Like this?

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.853
- You gonna do this right now?
- Very nice, you see?

00:01:16.853 --> 00:01:18.030
You did really well.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.380
So you do that every day--

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:20.910
- Every day?

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:21.743
- For half an hour
(audience laughs)

00:01:21.743 --> 00:01:23.531
to an hour, okay?

00:01:23.531 --> 00:01:25.064
- Oh, okay.
- Yeah!

00:01:25.064 --> 00:01:25.920
- Hm?

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.383
- Oh, you couldn't be tired already,

00:01:27.383 --> 00:01:28.216
come on now.
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:01:28.216 --> 00:01:29.790
- Elmo's just kidding!

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:32.220
Thank you for the advice,
and congratulations.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.356
Congratulations, Ms. Kelly,

00:01:33.356 --> 00:01:35.820
on your new set here, it's wonderful!

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.218
- Thank you!
(audience cheers)

00:01:37.218 --> 00:01:39.927
Thank you so much!

00:01:39.927 --> 00:01:43.740
We love it here.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.200
So wait, I love being in
the same city as y'all now.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.220
I love New York.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:48.960
Thank you for the welcome party.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.201
This has been really cool!
(audience cheers)

00:01:50.201 --> 00:01:52.290
(Elmo laughs)

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:53.998
- Yeah, (laughs) yeah!

00:01:53.998 --> 00:01:55.143
- We're in same city.
- It's a good thing

00:01:55.143 --> 00:01:55.976
- Yeah, we're in

00:01:55.976 --> 00:01:56.809
the same city now.
- That's right, yeah.

00:01:56.809 --> 00:01:58.421
We are so excited to have you.

00:01:58.421 --> 00:01:59.254
Aren't we, Oscar, excited

00:01:59.254 --> 00:02:01.154
to have Kelly here?
- Excited is not the word

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:04.083
I would've used, but, yeah.
(audience laughs)

00:02:04.083 --> 00:02:07.089
- But we're really, we're happy
to welcome you to the city.

00:02:07.089 --> 00:02:08.100
And you know what?

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.180
To say welcome,

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.340
everybody at "Sesame
Street" all pitched in

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.780
and got you some things.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:13.740
- [Kelly] Oh, what are they?

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.570
- Direct from "Sesame Street."

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:16.890
- Is that what's hiding under here?

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:17.730
Is that what's been hiding?
- Yeah, take a look.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:19.590
- [Kelly] Okay wait, I'm gonna reveal.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:20.610
- [Elmo] It's a little gift basket

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:21.532
from all your friends at "Sesame"!

00:02:21.532 --> 00:02:22.365
- [Arnold] Wow.
(audience aahs)

00:02:22.365 --> 00:02:23.370
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.110
This is so sweet.

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:26.160
Okay, so wait,

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.410
we're gonna go to the,
this is really cool!

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.113
So I can put this up?
- Now, now, now, now.

00:02:30.113 --> 00:02:30.946
Just so you know,

00:02:30.946 --> 00:02:33.576
that's not the sign.
(audience laughs)

00:02:33.576 --> 00:02:35.235
But it's a sign.

00:02:35.235 --> 00:02:37.380
(Kelly laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.630
- I need to watch more
of your program! (laughs)

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:40.590
No, this is awesome.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:42.270
So I'm gonna put this up here.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:43.103
Is that okay?

00:02:43.103 --> 00:02:44.130
Can I be a part of
"Sesame Street" with you?

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.009
- Of course, anytime.

00:02:45.009 --> 00:02:46.770
- Okay, thank you.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:48.072
Okay, so wait, next we're gonna go

00:02:48.072 --> 00:02:51.510
to what an interesting little number, so--

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.390
- Oh, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:53.640
- Yeah, that's from me too.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.040
That's actually for Mr.
Tight Sleeves over here.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.524
I heard you had a new book.
(audience laughs)

00:02:57.524 --> 00:02:58.357
- Oh, you know what,

00:02:58.357 --> 00:02:59.190
I'm gonna pass this off,

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.780
this is for you.
- And that's

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:01.613
actually a bookmark.

00:03:01.613 --> 00:03:02.636
- This is nice!

00:03:02.636 --> 00:03:03.678
- Yeah.

00:03:03.678 --> 00:03:05.174
- [Oscar] Scratch and sniff, too.

00:03:05.174 --> 00:03:07.380
- Yuck!
- Scratch and sniff?

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:11.580
- Never lose your place, yep.
(audience applauds)

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.100
- [Kelly] Okay, wait, so--

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.537
- This smells terrible.
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:15.537 --> 00:03:16.710
- Oh, thank you.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.767
- Yeah, really, oh!
- He's like, "You're welcome."

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:20.340
(Kelly laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:21.360
- Wait, who are these?

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:22.233
Whose are these?

00:03:22.233 --> 00:03:23.400
What are these?

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:24.830
I like these.
- Wait a minute.

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:26.393
You look like a monster.

00:03:26.393 --> 00:03:27.226
- Yeah, okay!
- You look

00:03:27.226 --> 00:03:28.059
like a "Sesame Street" monster!

00:03:28.059 --> 00:03:28.892
- Not the first time I've been told, yeah.

00:03:28.892 --> 00:03:30.637
- [Elmo] No no no!
(audience laughs)

00:03:30.637 --> 00:03:31.697
It's a good--
- Let's try those on.

00:03:31.697 --> 00:03:33.210
- I want you in to try these on.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.680
Try that on, come on.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:35.700
You think you're good looking now,

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:36.533
wait a minute.

00:03:36.533 --> 00:03:38.339
(audience laughs)

00:03:38.339 --> 00:03:39.785
- Ay-yo!
- Exactly!

00:03:39.785 --> 00:03:41.113
- Hello!
- Exactly!

00:03:41.113 --> 00:03:41.946
(audience cheers)

00:03:41.946 --> 00:03:46.946
- I'll be back!

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:48.960
- Ready for Halloween.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:49.793
I like it.

00:03:49.793 --> 00:03:50.626
Wait, so I--

00:03:50.626 --> 00:03:52.560
- I should have had those
when I did "Terminator."

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.420
- I know, no, trust me,
(Elmo laughs)

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:56.460
your glasses were cool in that. (laughs)

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:57.330
All right, so wait, Elmo,

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:58.380
I hear that you have advice

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.460
for kids with teddy bears.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:00.293
So I have two kids.

00:04:00.293 --> 00:04:01.320
What's the advice?
- Well,

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.940
one of those teddy bears is for you,

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:04.590
and one of them is for Mr. Arnold.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.297
- Oh, okay, which one would you like?

00:04:06.297 --> 00:04:07.470
- Oh!
- You can pick.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:08.303
- This is one thing that--

00:04:08.303 --> 00:04:09.461
- I think this one, thank you.
- Okay, okay.

00:04:09.461 --> 00:04:11.193
- One of the things we
learn on "Sesame Street,"

00:04:11.193 --> 00:04:13.890
that is, if you're
feeling nervous or scared,

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:17.160
you could give a soft toy
that you love a big hug.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:17.993
- Oh!

00:04:17.993 --> 00:04:19.470
- You can put it on your belly and do,

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:22.200
it's called belly buddy breathing.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.220
- Okay.
- So you breathe,

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:24.911
and you do it too Oscar!

00:04:24.911 --> 00:04:26.243
Come on Oscar!
(Oscar grumbles)

00:04:26.243 --> 00:04:27.076
(audience laughs)

00:04:27.076 --> 00:04:28.260
- Okay, everybody breathe in

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:29.517
through your nose, like this. (inhales)

00:04:29.517 --> 00:04:31.110
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:32.220
- And then slowly breathe out

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:33.497
through your mouth.
(Kelly exhales)

00:04:33.497 --> 00:04:34.330
(Arnold coughs)

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:35.312
Come on Oscar, do it.

00:04:35.312 --> 00:04:36.618
- I don't have a nose.

00:04:36.618 --> 00:04:38.310
(Kelly laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.300
- That is interesting.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.781
- [Elmo] Well, breathe
through your ears, then!

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:42.720
(Elmo laughs)

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.308
- That's very interesting.

00:04:44.308 --> 00:04:46.230
- But that's just one of the ways

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:47.986
that we learn how to calm down.

00:04:47.986 --> 00:04:50.153
- That's really true. I
do this with my children.

00:04:50.153 --> 00:04:51.570
We do breathing exercises.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:52.560
It does really help,

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.887
even for 41 year olds having a rough day.

00:04:55.887 --> 00:04:57.540
Well, thank you so much, Elmo.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:58.717
Thank you, Oscar The Grouch! (claps)

00:04:58.717 --> 00:05:00.150
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.320
You can see your friends

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:04.740
on "Sesame Street"
anytime on Max, season 54.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:06.510
It premieres November 9th.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:08.160
All right, so Elmo, Elmo, Elmo,

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.326
did you wanna say something with Arnold?

00:05:09.326 --> 00:05:10.740
I heard that you might have something

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.212
you wanted say with Arnold?

00:05:12.212 --> 00:05:13.110
- Oh, yeah, oh!

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:15.248
You know what, can we do the,

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:17.190
can we cut to commercial together?

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:18.023
- Okay, okay, okay.

00:05:18.023 --> 00:05:20.010
- 'Cause Elmo kinda knows--
You're done with the segment,

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:21.774
I hear you, okay.
- Elmo knows TV lingo.

00:05:21.774 --> 00:05:23.273
Elmo's done a lot of shows, you know.

00:05:23.273 --> 00:05:26.700
So Elmo can cut to a
commercial with Mr. Arnold!

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:27.857
- I like it, okay, you ready, okay.

00:05:27.857 --> 00:05:29.899
- Ready!
- Okay, y'all can go.

00:05:29.899 --> 00:05:31.399
- We'll be back.

00:05:31.399 --> 00:05:32.232
- We'll be back.

00:05:32.232 --> 00:05:34.074
(audience cheers and applauds)

